.TH K6-MESH 1 "August 2026" "quadratic-minmax-limit" "k=6 p=13 mesh"
.SH NAME
k6-mesh \- start, soft-stop, and status for the p=13 k=6 orbit mesh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B k6-mesh
.BR start | stop | status | man | dash
.RI [ NAME ]
.P
.B k6-mesh stop --hard
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the gauged k=6 Max+ enumerator across the LAN mesh. Orbits are claimed
with
.I GAUGE_OUT/.lock_<tvidx>
and written as
.I orb<tvidx>.npy .
Resume is those npy files. Workers never steal an orbit another host has locked.
.P
.B Stop is always soft
unless
.B --hard
is given. Soft stop writes a flag under
.I $K6_ROOT/mesh_stop/
and workers that have not yet taken a lock skip new orbits. Any outer that
already holds
.I .lock_*
runs to completion and writes its npy. There is no SIGKILL of an in-flight
orbit on the default path.
.P
Starting one worker never stops another.
.SH NAMES
.TP
.B all
Every compute worker (and dash on start).
.TP
.B v100
soulkiller Tesla V100, 2 CUDA processes. Log: enum_p13_k6.log
.TP
.B nuka
RX 9070 XT via HIP/CuPy (WSL). Log: enum_p13_k6_nuka.log
.TP
.B orin
Jetson Orin Ampere sm_87, 1 CUDA process, GEN_CAP=8e6. Log: enum_p13_k6_orin.log
.TP
.B a380
jellyfin Intel Arc A380 SYCL emit + host test. Log: enum_p13_k6_a380.log
.TP
.B cpu44
Legacy role label, not a node: soulkiller runs 11 in-flight orbits × 4 inner
Numba/OMP threads (44 cores), CUDA hidden. Log: enum_p13_k6_cpu44.log
.TP
.B dash
HTTP dashboard on :8765.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start NAME
Make that worker runnable without un-stopping the others (if ALL is set,
it is converted into per-worker flags on everyone else) and launch it
if it is not already running.
.B start all
brings up dash, v100, nuka, orin, a380, cpu44.
.TP
.B stop NAME
Soft-soft stop of that worker only: write
.I mesh_stop/NAME
and wait until the process exits after finishing current orbit(s).
The rest of the mesh keeps claiming new orbs. Dummy lock starve is
.B not
used here (starve is mesh-wide).
.TP
.B stop all
Write
.I mesh_stop/ALL
and occupy unclaimed slots with STARVE-marked dummy locks so
.B old
workers that predate the flag still finish in-flight orbs and then
exit. Dummy locks are dropped only after those processes are gone;
in-flight (unmarked) locks are never removed.
.TP
.B stop --hard NAME
SIGTERM, then SIGKILL. Can leave a .lock_* without npy; the next start
drops stale locks.
.TP
.B status
One-line ETA plus pid alive/stopped for each name.
.TP
.B dash
Serve the dashboard in the foreground.
.TP
.B man
Show this page (
.B man -l k6-mesh.1
).
.SH DASHBOARD
.B http://127.0.0.1:8765/k6_dashboard.html
.P
The LAN is firewalled; from a laptop:
.P
.RS
ssh -L 8765:127.0.0.1:8765 nick@192.168.1.113
.RE
.P
Each worker card has
.B Start
and
.B Soft stop
. Start/stop of one card does not touch the others. Soft stop is the same
flag as
.B k6-mesh stop NAME .
The page is a single column under 600px with 44px tap targets.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B K6_ROOT
Default /mnt/storage/e1work/maxplus_p13
.TP
.B K6_CODE
Default .../scripts/maxplus_profile_enum
.TP
.B K6_HOST
Set by the launcher (v100, nuka, ...).
.TP
.B K6_BACKEND
cuda (V100/nuka/orin), sycl (a380), cpu (cpu44).
.TP
.B K6_STOP_DIR
Default $K6_ROOT/mesh_stop
.SH FILES
.I $K6_ROOT/k6_gpu_out/orb*.npy
.I $K6_ROOT/k6_tasks.pkl
.I $K6_ROOT/k6_resume.json
.I $K6_ROOT/mesh_stop/<NAME>
.I $K6_ROOT/mesh_pids/<NAME>.pid
.SH NOTES
lucky (192.168.1.82) is DNS only and is never used.
cpu44 and v100 share soulkiller: cpu44 sets CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES empty and
uses 11 orbits × 4 threads (44 of 88) so the V100 host process still has cores.
Remote workers sshfs the platter at
.I /home/nick/mnt/maxplus_p13
and need
.I ~/.ssh/mesh.config
(k6-mesh copies it if missing).
.P
.B man k6-mesh
after
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/k6-mesh.1
is installed, or
.B ./k6-mesh man
from the scripts directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
run_kgauged.py, k6_control.py, k6_dashboard.py
